1
00:00:03,903 --> 00:00:06,406
TOTEI UNIVERSITY KINDERGARTEN

2
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,842
113 centimeters.

3
00:00:08,975 --> 00:00:10,744
19.2 kilograms.

4
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:12,746
Next.

5
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,952
Don't move. Stay still.

6
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:20,754
Don't move. Stay still.

7
00:00:20,887 --> 00:00:22,022
Don't move.

8
00:00:22,455 --> 00:00:23,390
Stay still.

9
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:26,826
Don't get angry.
Kids like to imitate.

10
00:00:26,893 --> 00:00:28,561
I KNOW

11
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:30,230
Do you have a medical license?

12
00:00:30,296 --> 00:00:31,598
I do.

13
00:00:32,132 --> 00:00:33,566
Which university?

14
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,769
Cuba Cubanacan Medical University.

15
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:38,304
What's that? Is it real?

16
00:00:38,371 --> 00:00:39,606
Yes.

17
00:00:39,672 --> 00:00:40,540
Do you have money?

18
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:41,841
Yes, I do.

19
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:44,744
Right here. $8.

20
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:45,979
You're kidding.

21
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:47,047
Serious?

22
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:50,884
A doctor with no money
and no education.

23
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:52,118
Shut up!

24
00:00:55,455 --> 00:00:56,990
Mom!

25
00:00:57,791 --> 00:00:58,958
What's the matter?

26
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,028
What happened?

27
00:01:02,328 --> 00:01:04,364
What did you do?

28
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,366
A physical exam.

29
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:07,700
Apologize.

30
00:01:08,301 --> 00:01:09,369
Apologize?

31
00:01:09,502 --> 00:01:10,403
Apologize!

32
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:11,638
I decline.

33
00:01:11,838 --> 00:01:12,739
Excuse me?

34
00:01:12,872 --> 00:01:13,840
They're little punks.

35
00:01:13,973 --> 00:01:15,742
What did you just say?!

36
00:01:16,009 --> 00:01:17,143
Shut up!

37
00:01:17,811 --> 00:01:20,280
- Apologize.
- Please.

38
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:24,684
Principal Mikamo,
we're deeply sorry.

39
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:25,585
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

40
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:26,886
Dr. Daimon, apologize.

41
00:01:27,153 --> 00:01:27,987
Why?

42
00:01:28,054 --> 00:01:28,922
It's okay.

43
00:01:29,522 --> 00:01:31,758
I should be the one to apologize.

44
00:01:32,325 --> 00:01:33,860
Please sit down.

45
00:01:34,661 --> 00:01:36,129
Thank you...

46
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:37,697
On the floor?

47
00:01:40,366 --> 00:01:43,336
Doctors of the great
Totei University Hospital

48
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,939
conducted a physical exam for us.

49
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:49,843
I'm sorry that the children
were so rude to you.

50
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:54,414
I've dedicated my whole life
to preschool education

51
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:57,150
but I'm still groping blindly in the dark.

52
00:01:57,484 --> 00:01:58,551
It's very embarrassing.

53
00:01:58,685 --> 00:02:02,922
Not at all. Actually,
the one who's immature is...

54
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:05,492
Lunchtime. I'm leaving.

55
00:02:05,558 --> 00:02:06,860
One moment.

56
00:02:08,761 --> 00:02:12,599
This is a token of our
apology and appreciation.

57
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,234
Please.

58
00:02:15,768 --> 00:02:17,003
- A rack?
- We can't...

59
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:18,838
- Thanks.
- Dr. Daimon.

60
00:02:23,376 --> 00:02:25,612
I don't accept anything
less than $1,000.

61
00:02:32,752 --> 00:02:35,421
Our apologies once again.

62
00:02:35,955 --> 00:02:37,957
- We accept gratefully.
- We do?

63
00:02:42,428 --> 00:02:47,767
A freelance surgeon, our biggest nightmare
misled a young Totei surgeon.

64
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:49,002
Ruined him.

65
00:02:50,136 --> 00:02:53,439
Chairman Uchikanda is furious.

66
00:02:54,507 --> 00:02:56,776
I've never known

67
00:02:57,076 --> 00:02:59,579
such humiliation.

68
00:02:59,779 --> 00:03:01,681
My deepest apologies.

69
00:03:02,415 --> 00:03:05,118
What can we do?

70
00:03:05,418 --> 00:03:10,089
How can we appease
Chairman Uchikanda?

71
00:03:10,557 --> 00:03:14,627
Re-educate your senior surgeons.

72
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:18,965
Strong leadership will
repress dissidents.

73
00:03:22,135 --> 00:03:23,203
- Yes sir.
- That word.

74
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:26,539
I said don't use it.

75
00:03:29,442 --> 00:03:30,310
But...

76
00:03:31,611 --> 00:03:33,913
I don't know a stronger sign of respect

77
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:36,049
than "yes sir."

78
00:03:42,922 --> 00:03:44,023
Thank you.

79
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:45,892
We're sorry for troubling you.

80
00:03:55,501 --> 00:03:57,036
- Wow.
- How much?

81
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:05,044
THANK YOU, KIND DOCTORS

82
00:04:07,981 --> 00:04:09,282
THANK YOU, DR. HARA

83
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:10,750
Uh-oh.

84
00:04:11,784 --> 00:04:13,820
WE LOVE YOU, DR. MORMOTO

85
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:17,490
Touching, huh?

86
00:04:21,294 --> 00:04:22,428
Principal!

87
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:27,900
Move.

88
00:04:28,701 --> 00:04:30,703
Are you okay?
Can you hear me?

89
00:04:31,471 --> 00:04:33,106
- Mr. Principal!
- Checking pupils.

90
00:04:37,143 --> 00:04:37,977
Loss of consciousness.

91
00:04:43,383 --> 00:04:45,818
Impaired respiration. Ambulance!

92
00:04:48,087 --> 00:04:51,924
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

93
00:04:53,493 --> 00:04:56,729
We must never again lose a young surgeon.

94
00:04:56,996 --> 00:04:59,332
We have to re-educate our staff.

95
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:01,401
It's our fault.

96
00:05:01,901 --> 00:05:02,969
Our apologies, sir.

97
00:05:03,436 --> 00:05:05,805
When we were interns

98
00:05:06,506 --> 00:05:09,909
we respected the professors
first and foremost.

99
00:05:10,209 --> 00:05:11,411
We did everything

100
00:05:11,878 --> 00:05:13,346
we were told to do.

101
00:05:14,447 --> 00:05:19,452
But young surgeons these days
are difficult to handle.

102
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:26,592
But we mustn't give up on
educating our juniors.

103
00:05:27,794 --> 00:05:29,295
A wonderful thought.

104
00:05:29,362 --> 00:05:30,730
In order to do so

105
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:32,799
leaders must be well liked.

106
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:34,200
Absolutely.

107
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:37,937
To be well liked,
we must listen to

108
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,239
our subordinates' opinions.

109
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,674
Like I do.

110
00:05:43,109 --> 00:05:46,946
You're a role model for all doctors.

111
00:05:47,113 --> 00:05:49,048
The worst thing you could do...

112
00:05:50,683 --> 00:05:52,151
- Dr. Inomata...
- Yes?

113
00:05:52,585 --> 00:05:54,487
Is to snap at others.

114
00:05:56,122 --> 00:06:00,326
Patience fosters popularity
in our profession.

115
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:04,564
I believe I just said
something praiseworthy.

116
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:07,934
Where's your "yes sir"?"

117
00:06:08,401 --> 00:06:09,402
Yes sir...

118
00:06:09,469 --> 00:06:10,970
- Louder.
- Yes sir...

119
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:12,772
- Louder!
- Yes sir!

120
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:13,906
Say it right away!

121
00:06:13,973 --> 00:06:15,241
Yes sir!

122
00:06:15,308 --> 00:06:16,275
Right away!

123
00:06:16,476 --> 00:06:21,147
The deputy chief surgeons
will now make their rounds.

124
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:22,715
Excuse us...

125
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:24,951
Joint rounds!

126
00:06:25,151 --> 00:06:26,552
Hey, Ebina!

127
00:06:28,121 --> 00:06:29,288
Idiots.

128
00:06:29,489 --> 00:06:31,290
You snapped at them.

129
00:06:31,357 --> 00:06:32,725
What?

130
00:06:32,792 --> 00:06:34,026
I heard you.

131
00:06:34,093 --> 00:06:35,294
What did you hear?

132
00:06:37,096 --> 00:06:39,532
The man at the top should stay calm.

133
00:06:39,599 --> 00:06:41,734
I'm not at the top.

134
00:06:42,301 --> 00:06:45,405
I'm right here on your lap.
Meow.

135
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:46,439
Woof.

136
00:06:46,539 --> 00:06:47,440
Meow.

137
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,776
Inappropriate.

138
00:06:49,842 --> 00:06:51,577
- Compliance.
- What?

139
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:54,547
I read between the lines.

140
00:06:55,047 --> 00:06:57,350
You're too slow, stupid!

141
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:00,153
I yelled. Sorry.

142
00:07:00,987 --> 00:07:02,355
<i>In 2017</i>

143
00:07:03,723 --> 00:07:08,661
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

144
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:15,034
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

145
00:07:17,236 --> 00:07:21,941
<i>In the midst of reform, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

146
00:07:22,842 --> 00:07:26,846
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

147
00:07:27,747 --> 00:07:29,449
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

148
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:32,985
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

149
00:07:33,352 --> 00:07:34,787
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

150
00:07:35,254 --> 00:07:40,359
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

151
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,061
Get out of the way.

152
00:07:44,931 --> 00:07:45,765
Move.

153
00:07:45,865 --> 00:07:46,699
Hey!

154
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,468
Daimon!

155
00:07:49,068 --> 00:07:50,036
How dare you!

156
00:07:50,336 --> 00:07:51,604
Sorry, sir.

157
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:55,708
Dr. Inomata snapped already.

158
00:07:56,442 --> 00:07:58,578
That woman makes everybody snap.

159
00:07:59,078 --> 00:08:00,513
But not us.

160
00:08:00,613 --> 00:08:01,547
Of course not.

161
00:08:02,081 --> 00:08:04,116
Did you say something?

162
00:08:09,689 --> 00:08:10,923
That patient...

163
00:08:12,091 --> 00:08:14,060
CT and an echo.
Straight away.

164
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:16,963
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

165
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:18,197
<i>Also known as...</i>

166
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:20,399
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

167
00:08:31,577 --> 00:08:33,045
A lung tumor.

168
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:35,615
Yes.

169
00:08:36,949 --> 00:08:39,118
- You knew?
- Yes.

170
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,987
Why haven't you had surgery?

171
00:08:41,654 --> 00:08:43,456
My primary care physician

172
00:08:44,156 --> 00:08:47,293
suggested chemotherapy
rather than surgery.

173
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,896
Did he really? Who's the quack?

174
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,464
Quack?

175
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,665
Let me cut it out.

176
00:08:53,266 --> 00:08:55,568
If we operate now, you'll be cured.

177
00:08:56,402 --> 00:08:58,204
Now?

178
00:08:59,438 --> 00:09:00,373
Not yet.

179
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:03,376
- Why?
- He's my patient.

180
00:09:05,177 --> 00:09:06,212
Your opinion?

181
00:09:06,345 --> 00:09:08,381
Stage 3A lung adenocarcinoma.

182
00:09:09,081 --> 00:09:11,517
Currently undergoing chemo
as an outpatient.

183
00:09:12,618 --> 00:09:14,954
Mediastinal lymph node metastasis.

184
00:09:15,087 --> 00:09:18,157
The tumor has to be shrunk before surgery.

185
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,559
I can do it.

186
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:23,229
A careless diagnosis by a part-timer.

187
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:30,736
Surgery without considering
the options is outdated.

188
00:09:32,338 --> 00:09:34,674
Where did you get your degree?

189
00:09:35,808 --> 00:09:39,912
A diagnosis should be made
carefully and deliberately.

190
00:09:40,146 --> 00:09:41,280
Dr. Inomata...

191
00:09:41,347 --> 00:09:43,049
What? Sorry about that.

192
00:09:43,783 --> 00:09:48,754
If you don't mind, I'd like to seek

193
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:52,158
a second opinion at another hospital.

194
00:09:52,658 --> 00:09:54,260
Second opinion?

195
00:09:54,393 --> 00:10:00,766
It's not that I don't trust
your diagnosis.

196
00:10:02,134 --> 00:10:06,038
But even after half a year of chemo

197
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:10,009
the tumor isn't shrinking.

198
00:10:10,676 --> 00:10:11,510
Is that true?

199
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:18,484
I understand.

200
00:10:19,251 --> 00:10:22,722
There are many hospitals out there.

201
00:10:24,857 --> 00:10:29,362
You should get their opinions
until you're satisfied.

202
00:10:30,196 --> 00:10:31,564
Thank you.

203
00:10:46,112 --> 00:10:47,046
Hello.

204
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,147
Hello.

205
00:10:51,617 --> 00:10:52,518
Hello.

206
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:56,222
- Second opinion?
- Yeah.

207
00:10:56,288 --> 00:10:59,492
Many patients nowadays
want a second opinion.

208
00:10:59,558 --> 00:11:01,494
Many doctors also advocate it.

209
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:02,895
But Dr. Inomata

210
00:11:02,962 --> 00:11:06,298
wants patients to heed to their doctors.

211
00:11:06,365 --> 00:11:08,634
I bet he snapped.

212
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:12,104
I agree. The type I hate most.

213
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:14,774
I'm surprised he allowed it.

214
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:17,977
Maybe he's surprisingly
a man of character.

215
00:11:18,077 --> 00:11:19,011
Out of the question.

216
00:11:19,278 --> 00:11:22,815
He's from a family of
pure Totei disciples.

217
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:26,552
Everybody has a medical
degree from Totei.

218
00:11:26,752 --> 00:11:31,557
In other words, a family that
cherishes honor and status.

219
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:34,460
So if a patient hurts his pride

220
00:11:34,727 --> 00:11:38,497
he might put pressure
on other hospitals.

221
00:11:39,131 --> 00:11:40,433
What kind of pressure?

222
00:11:40,566 --> 00:11:44,003
Like, tell them not to accept the patient.

223
00:11:44,070 --> 00:11:47,606
No... Would he go that far?

224
00:11:47,673 --> 00:11:49,675
He's a Totei professor after all.

225
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:50,810
Yeah.

226
00:11:52,745 --> 00:11:53,713
Excuse me.

227
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:56,315
Mr. Principal?

228
00:11:56,782 --> 00:11:57,850
What's the matter?

229
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:01,387
I was rejected by them all.

230
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:05,958
See?

231
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:09,695
They said there could be
no mistake in a diagnosis

232
00:12:10,229 --> 00:12:12,631
by Dr. Inomata of
Totei University Hospital.

233
00:12:12,765 --> 00:12:14,834
So he did pull some strings.

234
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:18,504
I didn't know a doctor could
be so underhanded.

235
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:21,640
Yes. "Riichi."

236
00:12:22,475 --> 00:12:23,609
For real?

237
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,444
Is that why you're here?

238
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:26,612
Yes.

239
00:12:26,879 --> 00:12:28,547
I heard you have outstanding doctors

240
00:12:28,614 --> 00:12:33,552
who can cure patients that were
rejected by other hospitals.

241
00:12:33,619 --> 00:12:34,920
Oh?

242
00:12:35,454 --> 00:12:39,024
Name your price. I want a referral.

243
00:12:39,391 --> 00:12:43,229
I can certainly do that.

244
00:12:43,796 --> 00:12:45,765
Me! I'll operate.

245
00:12:46,031 --> 00:12:47,433
But you're a part-timer.

246
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:50,903
I'm a freelance surgeon.
An outstanding one.

247
00:12:53,038 --> 00:12:53,906
No!

248
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:55,074
Don't discard that.

249
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:56,876
Very dangerous.

250
00:12:57,176 --> 00:12:59,211
- This?
- Don't discard it.

251
00:12:59,712 --> 00:13:02,081
Really? I think it's safe.

252
00:13:02,314 --> 00:13:03,883
Yeah, it's safe.

253
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:05,251
That's it!

254
00:13:05,317 --> 00:13:08,454
Ron. It's "kokushi,"
one of the highest hands.

255
00:13:09,722 --> 00:13:14,193
That's what you get for not listening to
his second opinion.

256
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:15,427
You're so right.

257
00:13:15,494 --> 00:13:18,063
- How dare you?
- Whoa.

258
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,165
This is bullshit!

259
00:13:19,231 --> 00:13:20,900
She snapped. Scary.

260
00:13:32,378 --> 00:13:37,249
Do you know what's most important
between a doctor and a patient?

261
00:13:37,516 --> 00:13:38,484
What is it?

262
00:13:38,918 --> 00:13:39,752
Love?

263
00:13:39,885 --> 00:13:42,655
Unfortunately, it's not love.

264
00:13:43,856 --> 00:13:48,260
Although between you and me,
love is the most important.

265
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,529
Ah, you're so sweet.

266
00:13:50,863 --> 00:13:54,433
I don't get your intention
behind that question.

267
00:13:54,733 --> 00:14:00,372
Do you want a respectable answer
like "relationship based on trust"?

268
00:14:01,874 --> 00:14:06,445
I see, pressure-free generation
like you are hard to deal with.

269
00:14:06,612 --> 00:14:08,647
So what's important?

270
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:12,484
Deference.

271
00:14:13,819 --> 00:14:18,324
The most important thing
is absolute deference.

272
00:14:18,557 --> 00:14:20,759
A patient's deference
to his doctor.

273
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,461
Ooh, scary...

274
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:25,297
If you want to be a successful doctor,

275
00:14:25,965 --> 00:14:27,833
don't let patients underestimate you.

276
00:14:29,268 --> 00:14:33,239
Dismiss the ones
who want a second opinion.

277
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:34,874
Actually,

278
00:14:36,275 --> 00:14:38,911
I'm also against second opinions.

279
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:41,280
Good. You get it.

280
00:14:42,081 --> 00:14:44,350
The earlier the treatment, the better.

281
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:47,853
A patient could become incurable

282
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:51,557
while he's running around
seeking a second opinion.

283
00:14:52,491 --> 00:14:53,893
Yes, I see.

284
00:14:53,959 --> 00:14:56,095
In any case,

285
00:14:56,328 --> 00:14:58,297
- what is this gathering's theme?
- Theme?

286
00:14:58,464 --> 00:15:02,401
If you're trying to solicit us
to join a faction...

287
00:15:02,501 --> 00:15:03,335
Faction?

288
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:04,303
Dr. Inomata,

289
00:15:05,437 --> 00:15:07,406
I have to get going.

290
00:15:07,773 --> 00:15:08,774
Hey, wait.

291
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,109
You're leaving already?

292
00:15:10,175 --> 00:15:11,410
I have to go too.

293
00:15:11,844 --> 00:15:12,711
Thank you.

294
00:15:12,945 --> 00:15:13,779
You're leaving?

295
00:15:16,715 --> 00:15:19,118
You're not very popular.

296
00:15:19,318 --> 00:15:20,986
Not at all.

297
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:25,257
Who needs a theme for a drink, idiots!

298
00:15:26,025 --> 00:15:28,494
Oh no... don't snap, no snap...

299
00:15:30,396 --> 00:15:33,165
Director, I want a wallet.

300
00:15:33,299 --> 00:15:34,266
Wallet?

301
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:39,038
You can have mine.
My favorite for years.

302
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:41,874
It's not what I had in mind.

303
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:45,244
It's crocodile. A fine wallet.

304
00:15:45,311 --> 00:15:46,345
I want a sparkly one.

305
00:15:46,812 --> 00:15:49,748
What a nice wallet.

306
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:53,419
I'll be happy to take the contents.

307
00:15:53,485 --> 00:15:57,957
You can't have the money
or the wallet.

308
00:15:58,023 --> 00:15:59,258
Too bad.

309
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:02,061
I'll get the documents.

310
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,595
Thank you.

311
00:16:08,033 --> 00:16:11,070
I don't like surprise visits.

312
00:16:11,203 --> 00:16:12,404
I'm sorry.

313
00:16:12,538 --> 00:16:13,472
What do you want?

314
00:16:13,605 --> 00:16:18,510
I was hoping to deposit a patient.

315
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:19,979
Deposit?

316
00:16:20,279 --> 00:16:22,114
What are we? A pawn shop?

317
00:16:25,718 --> 00:16:26,652
I brought this.

318
00:16:27,553 --> 00:16:28,554
Take a look.

319
00:16:30,122 --> 00:16:31,690
PERVERSELY ARROGANT AS EVER

320
00:16:31,757 --> 00:16:33,158
TOTEI REJECTS SECOND OPINION

321
00:16:33,225 --> 00:16:34,827
PERVERSELY ARROGANT

322
00:16:35,194 --> 00:16:36,028
What's this?

323
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:38,297
Galley proof for a magazine.

324
00:16:38,731 --> 00:16:42,334
Many disgruntled patients now
go to magazines and social media

325
00:16:42,935 --> 00:16:46,572
instead of complaining
directly to the hospital.

326
00:16:46,638 --> 00:16:49,975
It's up to you, Director.

327
00:16:50,609 --> 00:16:52,945
You can suppress this.

328
00:16:53,612 --> 00:16:57,583
What are you trying to do?

329
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:01,120
Threaten me? Blackmail me?

330
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:02,855
Certainly not.

331
00:17:03,022 --> 00:17:04,890
I was wondering

332
00:17:05,424 --> 00:17:11,263
if you'd allow Daimon to operate
on a patient who was kicked out

333
00:17:11,597 --> 00:17:15,467
of this hospital by Dr. Inomata.

334
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,236
What are you talking about?

335
00:17:17,302 --> 00:17:21,807
Principal Mikamo of
Totei University Kindergarten.

336
00:17:22,741 --> 00:17:25,744
We didn't kick him out.

337
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:32,251
He didn't accept a diagnosis
presented by a Totei professor.

338
00:17:32,451 --> 00:17:34,353
He didn't want to stay.

339
00:17:34,486 --> 00:17:35,554
Ah, I see.

340
00:17:36,321 --> 00:17:39,024
I have something else.

341
00:17:40,459 --> 00:17:42,194
"Help our principal."

342
00:17:42,628 --> 00:17:45,798
"The children's tearful wish comes true."

343
00:17:46,999 --> 00:17:49,635
"Thank you, Director Hiruma."

344
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:55,140
"Thank you, Director Hiruma."

345
00:17:55,607 --> 00:17:58,077
If the surgery succeeds

346
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:02,881
I've arranged the publication of
this heartwarming article.

347
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:06,218
The choice is yours.

348
00:18:06,285 --> 00:18:09,855
You don't leave anything
to chance, do you?

349
00:18:10,055 --> 00:18:11,356
I'm humbled.

350
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:14,460
Let us begin
this week's pre-op conference.

351
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:18,497
First case. 60-year-old male.
Hisashi Mikamo.

352
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:22,301
Diagnosis is stage 3A
lung adenocarcinoma.

353
00:18:22,434 --> 00:18:25,804
A 7-cm tumor in S3 of
the right upper lobe.

354
00:18:25,871 --> 00:18:29,041
Enlarged hilar and mediastinal
lymph nodes.

355
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:31,543
Dr. Inomata's patient?

356
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:34,980
He sought a second opinion
from another hospital.

357
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:38,383
The lead surgeon...

358
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:40,552
Dr. Michiko Daimon.

359
00:18:40,986 --> 00:18:43,288
I'd like to appoint you.

360
00:18:44,022 --> 00:18:45,390
Yes sir.

361
00:18:47,659 --> 00:18:48,827
She said "yes sir."

362
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:50,129
Hold on, sir.

363
00:18:52,397 --> 00:18:55,601
Mr. Mikamo was my patient first.

364
00:18:55,934 --> 00:18:59,138
I know his condition better
than anybody.

365
00:19:02,207 --> 00:19:04,943
Well, Dr. Inomata...

366
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:09,448
A patient wants
a high-risk operation

367
00:19:10,015 --> 00:19:14,586
and there's a surgeon who says
she can handle it.

368
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:18,056
There's no reason not to go ahead with it.

369
00:19:18,123 --> 00:19:21,059
No matter who the primary
care physician is.

370
00:19:21,126 --> 00:19:23,729
This patient sought a second opinion.

371
00:19:24,963 --> 00:19:29,101
None of the other hospitals
contradicted my diagnosis.

372
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:31,670
In other words,

373
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:34,806
everybody agrees that I'm right.

374
00:19:34,873 --> 00:19:36,675
You pressured them.

375
00:19:36,808 --> 00:19:38,210
Shut up, part-timer!

376
00:19:38,277 --> 00:19:39,645
Dr. Inomata.

377
00:19:39,711 --> 00:19:41,780
Calm down.

378
00:19:42,581 --> 00:19:43,749
Don't snap.

379
00:19:44,917 --> 00:19:46,018
But Director Hiruma...

380
00:19:46,919 --> 00:19:51,290
If you insist that
I perform the operation

381
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,991
I'll do it.

382
00:19:53,258 --> 00:19:55,060
His gloves are off.

383
00:19:55,394 --> 00:19:57,095
It's a matter of pride.

384
00:19:57,229 --> 00:19:58,530
Let me think.

385
00:19:58,597 --> 00:19:59,598
Okay then.

386
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:01,900
I'll do it.

387
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:03,735
You'll fail.

388
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,804
I said shut up, part-timer!

389
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:07,472
Dr. Inomata.

390
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:10,142
I told you not to snap.

391
00:20:10,475 --> 00:20:13,579
Why do you two keep clashing?

392
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,414
Why don't we do this?

393
00:20:16,815 --> 00:20:19,184
You two operate together.

394
00:20:20,085 --> 00:20:22,087
Dr. Inomata, the lead surgeon.

395
00:20:22,588 --> 00:20:26,425
Dr. Michiko Daimon,
the first assistant.

396
00:20:26,959 --> 00:20:28,660
- I decline.
- That's not acceptable.

397
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:32,297
I, the next chief surgeon
of Totei University Hospital

398
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:34,900
will not operate with a part-timer.

399
00:20:35,634 --> 00:20:37,402
Get her out of here!

400
00:20:37,469 --> 00:20:38,470
Dr. Inomata!

401
00:20:39,071 --> 00:20:40,872
- Don't snap!
- He snapped.

402
00:20:41,306 --> 00:20:44,610
Who said you'll be
the next chief surgeon?!

403
00:20:44,676 --> 00:20:46,745
- He also snapped.
- I'm next!

404
00:20:46,812 --> 00:20:48,647
- Him too.
- They all snapped.

405
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:50,282
- Snap snap.
- Don't get excited.

406
00:20:51,216 --> 00:20:52,818
Are you snapping too?!

407
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:55,587
It's 5 PM. I'm leaving.

408
00:20:56,488 --> 00:20:57,723
What the hell!

409
00:20:57,956 --> 00:20:59,057
Daimon!

410
00:20:59,791 --> 00:21:00,926
Stop fooling around!

411
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,294
Daimon!

412
00:21:07,799 --> 00:21:08,667
There she is!

413
00:21:13,171 --> 00:21:16,675
Michiko Daimon,
we checked you out.

414
00:21:17,042 --> 00:21:19,578
They say you're
an excellent surgeon.

415
00:21:21,346 --> 00:21:22,614
Gee, thanks.

416
00:21:24,349 --> 00:21:27,419
Operate on our principal.

417
00:21:27,486 --> 00:21:28,920
Do it!

418
00:21:29,154 --> 00:21:30,622
Do it?!

419
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:33,258
He's a good singer.

420
00:21:33,892 --> 00:21:38,063
But he stopped singing because
his voice got hoarse.

421
00:21:38,697 --> 00:21:39,698
Hoarse voice?

422
00:21:40,198 --> 00:21:41,233
Take this.

423
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:44,336
OPERATION FEE

424
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:45,537
Operation fee?

425
00:21:45,671 --> 00:21:47,472
You want money, right?

426
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,374
We collected donations.

427
00:21:49,441 --> 00:21:51,777
Donations...

428
00:21:59,885 --> 00:22:02,454
I don't accept anything
less than $1,000.

429
00:22:02,954 --> 00:22:04,189
Out of my way.

430
00:22:04,256 --> 00:22:05,190
Move.

431
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:08,794
Why?! Why?!

432
00:22:09,227 --> 00:22:10,696
Corrupt doctor.

433
00:22:12,297 --> 00:22:14,166
$1,000 is too much.

434
00:22:25,410 --> 00:22:30,115
Why should I operate with
a part-timer like her?

435
00:22:31,583 --> 00:22:32,551
Dr. Inomata...

436
00:22:34,019 --> 00:22:36,054
Go ahead and eat.

437
00:22:36,388 --> 00:22:37,689
These steaks are good.

438
00:22:37,989 --> 00:22:38,990
No thank you.

439
00:22:42,394 --> 00:22:44,930
Michiko Daimon is also good.

440
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:48,867
A good surgeon.

441
00:22:50,902 --> 00:22:54,639
To remove a tumor like that

442
00:22:55,741 --> 00:22:59,077
it takes superhuman skills.

443
00:23:01,246 --> 00:23:04,683
To protect your reputation
if anything else...

444
00:23:06,685 --> 00:23:08,587
Daimon should be there.

445
00:23:10,989 --> 00:23:14,292
You'll find her useful.

446
00:23:16,561 --> 00:23:19,998
Useful or not, that's not the point.

447
00:23:21,299 --> 00:23:26,638
As the next chief surgeon of
Totei University Hospital...

448
00:23:26,705 --> 00:23:27,739
What?

449
00:23:29,775 --> 00:23:30,776
Did you say "next?"

450
00:23:32,277 --> 00:23:33,311
Yes.

451
00:23:35,046 --> 00:23:36,248
Next, huh?

452
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:41,186
Maybe second next.

453
00:23:43,388 --> 00:23:44,222
Or...

454
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:49,694
Maybe even third next.

455
00:23:50,495 --> 00:23:52,497
Maybe even never.

456
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:55,700
- What?
- "What?"

457
00:23:58,804 --> 00:23:59,805
Dr. Inomata...

458
00:24:00,639 --> 00:24:04,075
I thought you were smarter than this.

459
00:24:06,912 --> 00:24:10,649
Director, I don't understand
what you're getting at.

460
00:24:10,916 --> 00:24:11,817
You don't?

461
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:15,487
Listen to me.

462
00:24:18,356 --> 00:24:23,595
There are no guarantees in surgery.

463
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:26,965
Not even for Michiko Daimon.

464
00:24:30,335 --> 00:24:35,106
I thought I told the three of you.

465
00:24:36,107 --> 00:24:38,977
Crush Michiko Daimon.

466
00:24:45,517 --> 00:24:47,819
Director Hiruma, are you...

467
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:53,658
telling me to fail intentionally
and blame it on Daimon?

468
00:24:56,661 --> 00:24:58,497
Don't be ridiculous.

469
00:25:01,132 --> 00:25:06,471
I'm the humble director of
Totei University Hospital

470
00:25:07,372 --> 00:25:09,941
whose top priority is the patients' lives.

471
00:25:11,810 --> 00:25:14,513
Watch what you say.

472
00:25:15,213 --> 00:25:16,314
I'm sorry.

473
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:20,018
Watch what you say or else...

474
00:25:21,953 --> 00:25:23,255
it'll be your downfall.

475
00:25:32,097 --> 00:25:33,598
I read between the lines.

476
00:25:33,932 --> 00:25:34,900
That's right.

477
00:25:43,608 --> 00:25:44,910
Let me cut it.

478
00:25:45,076 --> 00:25:46,344
No.

479
00:25:46,511 --> 00:25:49,414
Dr. Inomata was appointed
lead surgeon.

480
00:25:49,481 --> 00:25:51,149
Then the patient will die.

481
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:52,183
What?

482
00:25:52,817 --> 00:25:54,019
You'll die.

483
00:25:54,085 --> 00:25:55,353
No, before that.

484
00:25:56,154 --> 00:25:59,324
Dr. Inomata is going to
operate on me?

485
00:26:00,091 --> 00:26:00,926
Yes.

486
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:02,561
I'm so glad.

487
00:26:02,761 --> 00:26:03,628
You are?

488
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:05,797
I sought second opinions

489
00:26:05,864 --> 00:26:10,802
so I thought Dr. Inomata
brushed me off.

490
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:15,807
Being under the care of
a Totei professor-doctor

491
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:17,442
is reassuring.

492
00:26:18,710 --> 00:26:19,678
Excuse me.

493
00:26:21,279 --> 00:26:22,347
Thank God.

494
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:25,717
Patients are self-centered.

495
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:31,122
He's a good singer.

496
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:35,393
But he stopped singing because
his voice got hoarse.

497
00:26:40,465 --> 00:26:42,500
Feeling defeated for once?

498
00:26:43,668 --> 00:26:44,703
I need a favor.

499
00:26:56,314 --> 00:26:59,317
To protect your reputation
if anything else...

500
00:26:59,384 --> 00:27:01,019
Daimon should be there.

501
00:27:01,086 --> 00:27:03,888
CHEIF SURGEON'S OFFICE

502
00:27:13,999 --> 00:27:18,803
There are no guarantees in surgery.

503
00:27:19,204 --> 00:27:21,239
Not even for Michiko Daimon.

504
00:27:29,814 --> 00:27:31,016
Nonsense.

505
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:36,755
After all, I'm a surgeon of
Totei University Hospital.

506
00:27:49,634 --> 00:27:53,104
Is the principal glad to have
Dr. Inomata back?

507
00:27:54,472 --> 00:27:57,776
What an opportunist.
He was here begging for our help.

508
00:27:57,842 --> 00:27:59,010
Yeah, really.

509
00:27:59,144 --> 00:28:02,347
Does he know who to thank
for his upcoming operation?

510
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:05,183
I better charge them a lot extra.

511
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:10,321
Dr. Daimon...

512
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:12,123
Your turn.

513
00:28:13,725 --> 00:28:14,959
Sorry.

514
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:18,329
Are you worried about something?

515
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:19,698
Sort of.

516
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:22,200
Good evening.

517
00:28:22,967 --> 00:28:25,003
- Oh.
- It's been a while.

518
00:28:26,237 --> 00:28:29,107
I'm surprised you're here.

519
00:28:29,174 --> 00:28:30,475
I used a navigation app.

520
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,743
That's not what I meant.

521
00:28:32,610 --> 00:28:37,382
You're Dr. Morimoto who
aspired to be like Michiko

522
00:28:37,515 --> 00:28:42,153
and went overseas but
came back gaining nothing.

523
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:48,359
A third-class surgeon that was
banished to the boonies.

524
00:28:48,493 --> 00:28:49,894
Why all this bitterness?

525
00:28:50,028 --> 00:28:51,996
Sorry. He's just being mean.

526
00:28:53,264 --> 00:28:54,733
Let me see the test results.

527
00:28:55,166 --> 00:28:56,868
- Okay.
- No shoes.

528
00:28:56,968 --> 00:28:57,802
Sorry.

529
00:28:57,869 --> 00:28:59,738
You can hold him.

530
00:28:59,871 --> 00:29:03,274
So this is what's been
worrying Michiko.

531
00:29:05,643 --> 00:29:06,611
Akira...

532
00:29:09,447 --> 00:29:11,316
I thought this patient
had lung cancer.

533
00:29:11,616 --> 00:29:12,951
Just as I suspected.

534
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:14,953
This is rare.

535
00:29:17,255 --> 00:29:19,224
I'll take part in the surgery.

536
00:29:32,170 --> 00:29:35,640
You're here against my will.

537
00:29:35,807 --> 00:29:38,076
Just don't get in my way.

538
00:29:38,977 --> 00:29:41,646
You all, watch carefully
and learn something.

539
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:43,982
- Yes, Doctor.
- Let's do it.

540
00:29:44,415 --> 00:29:45,350
Ready?

541
00:29:53,958 --> 00:29:57,395
Starting the removal of
the right upper lobe

542
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:59,531
and mediastinal lymph nodes.

543
00:30:00,031 --> 00:30:01,432
Good luck, team.

544
00:30:01,599 --> 00:30:02,767
Thank you.

545
00:30:02,834 --> 00:30:06,905
Vitals. BP 110 over 76.
Pulse 75. Normal sinus rhythm.

546
00:30:07,405 --> 00:30:08,506
Scalpel.

547
00:30:18,183 --> 00:30:19,317
Monopolar.

548
00:30:34,065 --> 00:30:36,301
His skills are rather impressive.

549
00:30:36,367 --> 00:30:38,803
Yes. Not to be taken lightly.

550
00:30:39,437 --> 00:30:43,975
But I don't think the tumor is small
enough for complete removal.

551
00:30:44,809 --> 00:30:47,045
Let's see how he handles it.

552
00:30:56,821 --> 00:30:57,822
It's big.

553
00:30:59,123 --> 00:31:01,192
Firmly adhered to
the upper vena cava.

554
00:31:01,559 --> 00:31:04,762
Why is it so big after
half a year of chemo?

555
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:08,166
The drugs work differently
for each individual.

556
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,336
I doubt it's about the drugs.

557
00:31:12,237 --> 00:31:14,272
- What?
- You don't have the skills

558
00:31:14,606 --> 00:31:16,608
to remove it completely.

559
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:19,077
Watch me.

560
00:31:19,143 --> 00:31:19,978
Pean.

561
00:31:25,850 --> 00:31:27,085
It's too dangerous.

562
00:31:27,385 --> 00:31:29,320
Don't worry. No problem.

563
00:31:37,428 --> 00:31:38,763
Blood vessel damaged.
Suction.

564
00:31:39,063 --> 00:31:40,031
Starting suction.

565
00:31:49,574 --> 00:31:51,843
BP down in 60s.
Pulse 140.

566
00:31:52,043 --> 00:31:52,877
No problem.

567
00:31:53,011 --> 00:31:55,146
RBC, eight units. FFP too.

568
00:31:55,780 --> 00:31:57,181
A whole lot of problems.

569
00:32:03,154 --> 00:32:05,123
Upper pulmonary vein.
Ligature and excision.

570
00:32:06,324 --> 00:32:09,027
I know. You didn't have to tell me.

571
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:10,762
2-0 silk.

572
00:32:27,045 --> 00:32:29,747
Next, cut A1+3.

573
00:32:29,814 --> 00:32:32,250
That's right.
You know the procedure.

574
00:32:32,684 --> 00:32:33,618
Are you serious?

575
00:32:50,535 --> 00:32:52,971
Good. It's been handled.

576
00:32:53,037 --> 00:32:54,539
You did it, Dr. Inomata.

577
00:32:54,605 --> 00:32:56,708
Separating tumor from
right middle lobe.

578
00:32:56,841 --> 00:32:57,809
Pean.

579
00:33:00,979 --> 00:33:03,381
Dr. Daimon handled it.

580
00:33:04,215 --> 00:33:06,017
This is so educational.

581
00:33:06,851 --> 00:33:08,152
Of what not to do.

582
00:33:14,525 --> 00:33:15,393
Finished.

583
00:33:15,727 --> 00:33:18,096
The tumor has been completely removed.

584
00:33:18,296 --> 00:33:19,931
First Assistant, sutures.

585
00:33:20,231 --> 00:33:22,133
- I decline.
- What?

586
00:33:24,369 --> 00:33:25,870
The operation isn't finished.

587
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:29,107
What do you mean?

588
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:31,175
Move.

589
00:33:32,477 --> 00:33:33,478
Changing procedure.

590
00:33:34,278 --> 00:33:35,546
To what?

591
00:33:35,613 --> 00:33:37,015
You, suture.

592
00:33:38,316 --> 00:33:41,185
Now removing a tumor
in the thyroid.

593
00:33:41,786 --> 00:33:43,721
Thyroid tumor?

594
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:46,758
Could it be...?

595
00:33:47,258 --> 00:33:48,092
What's going on?

596
00:33:48,226 --> 00:33:51,195
The lung tumor was
a metastasis from the thyroid.

597
00:33:51,396 --> 00:33:53,097
The primary tumor is in the thyroid.

598
00:33:53,698 --> 00:33:56,534
That's why chemotherapy didn't work.

599
00:33:58,069 --> 00:33:59,537
What are you talking about?

600
00:34:00,605 --> 00:34:01,439
I...

601
00:34:02,073 --> 00:34:05,043
also never fail a second opinion.

602
00:34:07,478 --> 00:34:08,613
Do the sutures.

603
00:34:09,247 --> 00:34:10,114
Yes, Doctor.

604
00:34:11,082 --> 00:34:12,683
3-0 absorbable.

605
00:34:14,452 --> 00:34:17,088
Dr. Inomata missed the primary tumor.

606
00:34:17,955 --> 00:34:19,724
Occult thyroid carcinoma.

607
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:21,592
Occult carcinoma?

608
00:34:22,660 --> 00:34:25,163
A big metastatic tumor
is found first.

609
00:34:25,229 --> 00:34:28,766
A small primary tumor is
later found in the thyroid.

610
00:34:29,467 --> 00:34:30,501
A rare case.

611
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:37,942
This can't be happening.

612
00:34:38,643 --> 00:34:42,713
Thyroid papillary carcinoma
advances extremely slowly and

613
00:34:42,780 --> 00:34:45,116
lung metastasis of
a micropapillary carcinoma

614
00:34:45,783 --> 00:34:48,820
is difficult to differentiate
from primary lung cancer.

615
00:34:50,121 --> 00:34:51,155
Hence overlooked.

616
00:34:51,322 --> 00:34:53,491
How did Daimon find it?

617
00:34:54,158 --> 00:34:55,059
I don't know.

618
00:34:55,126 --> 00:34:57,728
According to Dr. Morimoto...

619
00:34:57,929 --> 00:35:02,667
Chemotherapy for lung cancer
didn't shrink the tumor.

620
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:05,670
Even after half a year of chemo

621
00:35:06,737 --> 00:35:09,540
the tumor isn't shrinking.

622
00:35:10,274 --> 00:35:11,576
And the change in his voice.

623
00:35:11,709 --> 00:35:16,114
Being under the care of a Totei
professor-doctor is reassuring.

624
00:35:17,415 --> 00:35:18,483
Excuse me.

625
00:35:18,983 --> 00:35:21,519
A tumor pressing against
the recurrent laryngeal nerve.

626
00:35:22,487 --> 00:35:26,491
So that's how Daimon diagnosed
the occult thyroid carcinoma.

627
00:35:26,991 --> 00:35:28,059
I believe so.

628
00:35:28,326 --> 00:35:33,197
I've come to realize what a daunting
surgeon Michiko Daimon is.

629
00:35:50,214 --> 00:35:52,517
Exposing isthmus. 11 blade.

630
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:59,056
Extracting right lobe. Metzen.

631
00:36:02,527 --> 00:36:05,196
- Second Assistant, pull the retractor.
- Yes, Doctor.

632
00:36:16,741 --> 00:36:18,009
Right lobe extracted.

633
00:36:18,309 --> 00:36:20,344
Hemostasis. Bipolar.

634
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:34,559
Finished.

635
00:36:34,625 --> 00:36:37,595
Blood loss 1,000 cc.
Vitals are normal.

636
00:36:45,636 --> 00:36:46,470
Good job.

637
00:36:46,837 --> 00:36:47,805
Good job.

638
00:36:48,172 --> 00:36:49,273
Good job.

639
00:36:58,282 --> 00:36:59,250
Occult carcinoma.

640
00:37:00,618 --> 00:37:01,786
That's impossible.

641
00:37:03,487 --> 00:37:04,922
I overlooked it?

642
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:09,460
He looks like he's possessed.

643
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:12,663
I know how it feels.

644
00:37:12,930 --> 00:37:17,268
My pride was brutally crushed
by Daimon many times.

645
00:37:18,002 --> 00:37:20,371
Dr. Inomata's first OR encounter
with Daimon.

646
00:37:20,938 --> 00:37:21,939
It's understandable.

647
00:37:31,882 --> 00:37:33,084
How did she find it?

648
00:37:34,652 --> 00:37:36,854
Why didn't I find it?!

649
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:10,021
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

650
00:38:20,331 --> 00:38:21,299
Dr. Inomata.

651
00:38:23,668 --> 00:38:25,369
You did well.

652
00:38:26,737 --> 00:38:28,873
- Sir...
- A case report.

653
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:32,143
Can you write one right away?

654
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:34,912
Case report?

655
00:38:35,446 --> 00:38:42,320
A small undetectable primary tumor
that metastasized into a big tumor.

656
00:38:43,754 --> 00:38:45,923
Occult thyroid carcinoma.

657
00:38:47,258 --> 00:38:51,529
It will be a remarkable article.

658
00:38:52,797 --> 00:38:55,966
But Daimon handled the surgery...

659
00:38:59,003 --> 00:39:00,137
So?

660
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:05,543
I have my pride as the next chief surgeon.

661
00:39:06,544 --> 00:39:07,378
So?

662
00:39:09,613 --> 00:39:14,985
I haven't been reduced to stealing
credit from a lowly part-timer.

663
00:39:19,423 --> 00:39:20,491
Did you hear that?

664
00:39:21,559 --> 00:39:25,563
I, the next chief surgeon,
will write the article.

665
00:39:26,063 --> 00:39:29,200
I, the next chief surgeon,
will write it.

666
00:39:30,835 --> 00:39:31,669
Is that right?

667
00:39:31,836 --> 00:39:36,507
Then Dr. Torii and Dr. Ebina...

668
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:41,412
You two Takashis can write it together.

669
00:39:43,013 --> 00:39:43,848
Wait, sir.

670
00:39:46,684 --> 00:39:50,154
I, Takashi Inomata, will write it.

671
00:39:51,622 --> 00:39:54,892
Now we're talking.
Very good.

672
00:39:55,025 --> 00:39:57,328
Your pride, is it?

673
00:39:57,762 --> 00:40:03,300
Entrust it to me for a while.
Every morsel of it.

674
00:40:03,901 --> 00:40:04,802
Yes sir.

675
00:40:07,838 --> 00:40:08,906
Hello, gentlemen.

676
00:40:12,309 --> 00:40:17,148
Thank you for employing Daimon
and Jonouchi from our agency.

677
00:40:17,481 --> 00:40:18,516
You're here already?

678
00:40:18,582 --> 00:40:20,084
Yes, already.

679
00:40:20,217 --> 00:40:21,318
Melon.

680
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:23,888
- The bill.
- Here it is.

681
00:40:24,288 --> 00:40:26,390
This always frightens me.

682
00:40:27,324 --> 00:40:30,795
Oh, the anxiety...
Bad for the heart.

683
00:40:30,861 --> 00:40:32,363
Heart attack.

684
00:40:33,464 --> 00:40:35,633
This is ruthless.

685
00:40:36,133 --> 00:40:37,368
$200,000

686
00:40:37,501 --> 00:40:38,769
So many zeros.

687
00:40:38,836 --> 00:40:42,740
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven...

688
00:40:42,873 --> 00:40:44,341
Mind-blowing.

689
00:40:44,909 --> 00:40:46,811
Daimon's fee?

690
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:51,949
Not Daimon.
This melon man gets most of it.

691
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:54,218
That's a disturbing remark.

692
00:40:54,685 --> 00:41:00,157
Daimon fixed Dr. Inomata's error
allowing him to save face.

693
00:41:00,825 --> 00:41:04,428
Moreover, she not only removed a big tumor

694
00:41:04,495 --> 00:41:08,666
but also discovered
and definitively excised

695
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:10,534
a tiny overlooked primary tumor.

696
00:41:10,901 --> 00:41:14,004
The blessings of a second opinion.

697
00:41:14,071 --> 00:41:16,507
Second opinion...

698
00:41:16,574 --> 00:41:17,408
Yes.

699
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:20,344
Considering everything

700
00:41:20,411 --> 00:41:24,915
I believe it's a very reasonable amount.

701
00:41:28,986 --> 00:41:29,887
But...

702
00:41:31,689 --> 00:41:35,359
you brought this patient to us.

703
00:41:36,227 --> 00:41:41,565
Don't we deserve a special
discount for that?

704
00:41:41,732 --> 00:41:42,766
No.

705
00:41:43,634 --> 00:41:49,273
However, I have something else
that you'll find extremely delightful.

706
00:41:50,774 --> 00:41:51,609
Other than the melon?

707
00:41:51,675 --> 00:41:52,510
Yes.

708
00:41:53,377 --> 00:41:54,812
Come on in!

709
00:41:55,145 --> 00:41:57,681
Okay!

710
00:42:02,987 --> 00:42:08,559
Hello, Director Hiruma.

711
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:10,394
Yes. Hello.

712
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:17,501
Mr. Mikamo is our principal.

713
00:42:18,035 --> 00:42:24,875
Thank you very much for saving his life.

714
00:42:25,409 --> 00:42:29,313
Director Hiruma, you are

715
00:42:29,947 --> 00:42:32,650
the hero of

716
00:42:32,783 --> 00:42:37,721
Totei University Kindergarten.

717
00:42:37,788 --> 00:42:41,759
Thank you.

718
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:46,597
Oh no... Many thanks to you too.

719
00:42:48,165 --> 00:42:51,869
Wow... Thank you.

720
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:54,004
You drew pictures.

721
00:42:54,438 --> 00:42:57,808
Chairman Uchikanda will
be so pleased to hear this.

722
00:42:59,310 --> 00:43:01,312
Hey, melon man.

723
00:43:01,445 --> 00:43:03,981
I'll be happy to pay $200,000.

724
00:43:04,048 --> 00:43:04,949
Yes sir.

725
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:07,985
Wonderful.

726
00:43:08,319 --> 00:43:09,820
$200,000!

727
00:43:12,323 --> 00:43:13,924
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

728
00:43:15,225 --> 00:43:19,129
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

729
00:43:20,130 --> 00:43:25,336
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

730
00:43:29,239 --> 00:43:33,777
Michiko Daimon, you didn't do
anything to save our principal.

731
00:43:35,546 --> 00:43:38,282
Dr. Inomata performed the surgery.

732
00:43:38,349 --> 00:43:41,285
As instructed by Director Hiruma.
Got it?

733
00:43:43,187 --> 00:43:44,421
Corrupt doctor!

734
00:43:44,888 --> 00:43:45,856
What?

735
00:43:46,090 --> 00:43:47,858
Corrupt doctor!

736
00:43:54,064 --> 00:43:55,399
CORRUPT DOCTOR

737
00:43:56,266 --> 00:43:59,570
Children are so innocent,
aren't they?

738
00:44:00,070 --> 00:44:02,239
I should start a kindergarten.

739
00:44:02,673 --> 00:44:03,574
Are you serious?

740
00:44:03,774 --> 00:44:08,112
Let's go, children.
Follow me.

741
00:44:08,178 --> 00:44:12,349
Let's go dance by the blue sea.

742
00:44:12,416 --> 00:44:13,684
Seaside Bound!

743
00:44:35,939 --> 00:44:38,142
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

744
00:44:38,809 --> 00:44:39,810
<i>Also known as...</i>

745
00:44:40,310 --> 00:44:42,012
"Doctor-X."

746
00:44:42,279 --> 00:44:47,284
Hey! No kindergarten! No way!

747
00:44:52,322 --> 00:44:55,626
No! Get away from me!

748
00:44:56,193 --> 00:44:57,161
Matchmaking party?

749
00:44:57,227 --> 00:44:58,996
It's amazing I met such a wonderful girl.

750
00:44:59,063 --> 00:45:00,831
Chairman Uchikanda's daughter?

751
00:45:00,898 --> 00:45:02,499
- If she loses her life.
- You're fired.

752
00:45:02,566 --> 00:45:04,134
I'll save your life.

753
00:45:04,201 --> 00:45:05,502
Surgeon, what's your plan?

754
00:45:05,569 --> 00:45:06,570
This is the limit.

755
00:45:06,637 --> 00:45:07,504
Inoperable.

756
00:45:07,571 --> 00:45:08,539
Abandon her?

757
00:45:08,605 --> 00:45:10,474
It's bigger!
